# Gill School OS — email (cPanel webmail) configuration.
# Copy to .env (next to server.js) or paste into the host panel's Environment
# Variables. Verification/reset codes and mailbox credentials are delivered by
# email only and require SMTP below — they are never shown on screen.
#
# The server/port/mailbox below are also the app's built-in defaults — the
# ONLY value you truly must provide is SMTP_PASS. Alternatively skip this file
# entirely and save the settings from Admin → Staff Accounts → "School email
# (SMTP) status" (stored in DATA_DIR/mail.json, git-ignored; saved settings
# override these variables).
#
# 1. In cPanel/Webuzo → Email Accounts, create: noreply@gill.ac.ug (+ one
#    mailbox per staff member, e.g. a.hassan@gill.ac.ug).
# 2. In cPanel → Email Accounts → Connect Devices, copy the SMTP host/port.
#    Typical cPanel values: mail.gill.ac.ug, port 465 with SSL/TLS.
# 3. Full walkthrough: docs/email-setup.md

# --- cPanel SMTP (outgoing mail: invites, codes, resets, receipts) ---
SMTP_HOST=mail.gill.ac.ug
SMTP_PORT=465
SMTP_SECURE=true
SMTP_USER=noreply@gill.ac.ug
SMTP_PASS=change-me-to-the-mailbox-password
SMTP_FROM=Gill School OS <noreply@gill.ac.ug>

# --- Public portal address printed inside email links ---
APP_URL=https://portal.gill.ac.ug

# --- Branded webmail URL printed in personalised-mailbox emails ---
# WEBMAIL_URL=https://webmail.gill.ac.ug:2003/

# --- Optional: Webuzo/cPanel API for automatic mailbox provisioning ---
# Only needed for "Send personalised email" (Bursar → Fees → School emails)
# to CREATE the family mailbox itself. Leave unset and the mailbox is created
# by hand in Webuzo -> Email Accounts first (exactly like staff mailboxes).
# WEBUZO_API_URL=https://nexus.crystalcloudhost.com:2083
# WEBUZO_API_TOKEN=cpuser:your-cpanel-uapi-token

# --- Only this domain can hold staff portal accounts ---
STAFF_EMAIL_DOMAIN=gill.ac.ug

# --- Shared hosting (see docs/deploy-shared-hosting.md) ---
# PORT is assigned by the panel's Node.js app manager (the app reads it).
# DATA_DIR (optional) keeps the live database outside the app folder so
# redeploys can never wipe school data. NODE_ENV should be production.
# PORT=30008
# DATA_DIR=/home/gillacug/portal-data
# NODE_ENV=production
